  "report": "## Denominator provenance\n\n1. **80 primary candidates: invalid denominator.** The action plan says they may be renamed, merged, rejected or replaced and are not commitments.\n2. **100 portfolio rows: useful proxy, not proven frozen workflow inventory.** It includes 20 reserves chosen partly for the 157-tool count, six impossible/replaced concepts, and dedicated-tool granularity rather than comparable outcomes.\n3. **94 non-replacement rows: smallest auditable proxy available today.** This is 100 minus six replacement rows. Latest state is 71 qualified + 4 implemented-unverified + 3 candidate + 16 probe-required.\n4. **259 competitor rows / 106 signatures: parity denominator only.** The report explicitly says covered-contract and witness-file presence do not imply behavior or live qualification. Multiple source names consolidate into one contract, so neither 259 nor 106 is the Creator workflow denominator.\n5. **P2-P6 child queues: closer to frozen requirements but not reconciled into one inventory.** P2 has 28 original requirements versus 22 primary rows; P6 has 16 versus 12. P3/P4/P5 use 16/16/10. These already prove that portfolio arithmetic silently drops or merges requirements unless an explicit mapping is published.\n6. **Missing data:** no artifact with the required workflow-row schema, official-source provenance, frozen row count, P0 flags, per-domain denominator, implementation state and accepted composition recipe was found. Therefore an exact >=90% Creator workflow percentage is presently unknowable.\n\n## Compact matrix — all 23 non-qualified portfolio rows\n\n| Row | Honest status | Existing composition / exact remaining behavior | Priority |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| animationGraphEdit | Missing | No registered bounded graph editor found. Need persistent state/transition/variable/mask mutation independent of panel state, round-trip/read-back and rollback. | P0 |\n| animationGraphPreview | Partial by composition | runtime sessions and animation controls exist, but no graph-specific run with parameter changes, observed transitions and ordered events tied to one named session. | P0 |\n| animationRetargetValidate | Only-test-pending for its narrowed contract | Implemented joint/skeleton/clip metadata comparison; fails closed when joint metadata is absent and explicitly does not retarget. Needs suitable positive fixture and negative evidence. | P2 |\n| skeletalAnimationPlay | Complete-by-existing-composition, pending contract adapter/evidence | animationRuntimeControl supports Spine/DragonBones play, pause, resume and stop. Missing queued semantics: queue operation, named runtime session identity, and state confirmation under that session. If queue remains mandatory this is Partial, not complete. | P0 |\n| skeletalAnimationEvents | Missing | No bounded ordered Spine/DragonBones event collector tied to one playback session. | P1 |\n| audioPlaybackControl | Missing | AudioSource configuration exists, but no runtime play/pause/stop/seek contract with state confirmation. | P0 |\n| audioPlaybackObserve | Missing | No bounded progress/state observation with activation/load errors. | P0 |\n| physics2dConfigure | Unsupported on 3.7.3 route | Registered wrapper delegates to projectSetConfig; plan records project/set-config unavailable. Need a verified settings writer for backend and collision matrix plus read-back, or keep explicit unsupported with zero credit. | P1 |\n| physics3dConfigure | Unsupported on 3.7.3 route | Same limitation; need backend-aware settings mutation/read-back or zero credit. | P1 |\n| particleConfigure | Missing | No dedicated typed module/curve/gradient mutation implementation found. Need persistent component read-back. | P1 |\n| renderConfigurationApply | Missing | No dedicated implementation found. Need atomic camera/light/fog/skybox application, scene read-back, failure recovery and visual postcondition. | P0 |\n| renderDiagnosticsCollect | Missing | No target-identified bounded frame/render sampler found. Screenshot/runtime state alone does not provide frame/render diagnostics. | P1 |\n| lightBakeManage | Missing/unsupported pending probe | Need real finite bake job start/status/cancel/terminal lifecycle and generated output asset witness; panel clicks cannot count. | P2 |\n| terrainEdit | Missing/unsupported pending probe | Need supported bounded height/layer mutation with reopen persistence; raw unpublished asset-byte editing is forbidden. | P1 |\n| localizationInspect | Partial | Existing handler reports package availability, current language, languages and direction. It does not discover compiled tables or resource mappings required by the row. | P1 |\n| localizationTableEdit | Missing | No persistent documented-package table mutation implementation found. | P1 |\n| localizationValidate | Partial, not merely test-pending | Current implementation validates existence of 1–256 keys in only the current language via l10n.exists. Missing cross-language comparison, fallback gaps, glyph/font availability and layout-overflow risks in compiled resources. The child plan explicitly says no accepted scope reduction. | P0 |\n| localizationPreview | Missing | No locale switch workflow with acknowledged runtime restart/session replacement and visual/read-back evidence. | P1 |\n| previewSessionStart | Complete-by-existing-composition with limitation | runtimePreviewControl starts Creator preview; runtimeSessionLifecycle then attaches only when game-view state is valid. A composed recipe can satisfy start + verified identity if made atomic/reproducible. Current session lifecycle itself does not start preview and supports only game-view. | P0 |\n| previewSessionStop | Complete-by-existing-composition with limitation | runtimePreviewControl stops preview, while lifecycle stop only marks local session stopped and throws RUNTIME_CONTROL_UNAVAILABLE. Need an atomic recipe that proves target termination and reconciles/removes local session state. | P0 |\n| previewResolutionSet | Unsupported on Creator 3.7.3 | Implementation calls preview/set-resolution and fails with UNSUPPORTED_PREVIEW_IPC. No functioning workflow credit. | P2 |\n| prefabApplyOverrides | Only-test-pending structurally, but known runtime failure | Typed operation and source/instance read-back exist. Recorded writable fixture returned “Failed to apply prefab”. Minimum work is diagnose/fix the actual apply route and prove source/instance result; not just add a test. | P0 |\n| prefabRevertOverrides | Partial | Full-instance restore exists with read-back. Any non-empty paths request is deliberately rejected as UNSUPPORTED_SELECTIVE_REVERT. Frozen row requires selected overrides, so selective revert remains missing. Either implement selective restoration through typed property recovery or obtain explicit scope amendment; full restore alone cannot close it. | P0 |\n\n## Broader limitations that must remain visible\n\n- **animationRuntimeControl:** useful existing composition for generic Animation and skeletal playback/state/cache. It does not implement graph authoring/transition observation, event collection, audio playback, or session identity. The latest audit marks its live suites failed on the sampled endpoint; that is qualification status, not proof that source is absent.\n- **runtimePreviewControl:** source implements start/pause/resume/stop/step/state, but calls Creator preview IPC directly and returns success for mutation calls without independent termination/readiness postconditions. runtimeSessionLifecycle provides identity/readiness but its stop/reset are explicitly local-only failures. Compose the two; do not count either raw registration as the full start/stop workflow.\n- **runtime state seam:** readState constructs running:true whenever a state payload exists. Per the assignment constraint, this must not be used alone as proof that preview is genuinely running.\n- **P2 frozen limitations beyond the 23 rows:** assetManifestExport’s original hashes/exclusions are split with assetCatalogManifest; assetUsageAnalyze was only an open-scene probe before later graph work and needs explicit mapping; tilemapValidate had UUID-focused rather than complete gid/dimension validation; sprite atlas evidence lacked frames; uiResponsivePreview used deterministic projected rectangles rather than rendered multi-resolution comparison; native reference-image transforms remained unavailable. Qualified ledger labels do not erase these contract deltas.\n- **P3:** skeletalAnimationConfigure’s qualified scope is playOnLoad/useBakedAnimation, not the originally described skin/mix/socket setup. animationRuntimeControl is outside the frozen child queue and cannot be counted twice.\n- **P5:** materialEdit still lacks required rendered visual postcondition. renderPipelineInspect is bounded native read-back, not normalized pass/camera/layer compatibility diagnostics.\n- **P6:** assetBundleValidate was metadata-only in source evidence unless actual runtime load/release has since been separately proven; build artifact inventory and diagnostics availability must not be confused with the original terminal-build/hash/target contract.\n\n## Can >=90% be evidenced today?\n\n**No.**\n\n- Exact workflow denominator: unavailable.\n- Best auditable proxy: 94 non-replacement portfolio rows.\n- Optimistic implemented numerator: 75, yielding **79.8%**.\n- Strict numerator after treating localizationValidate and selective prefab revert as partial, and prefab apply as known failing, is at most 72/94 = **76.6%** before reviewing other narrowed “qualified” rows.\n- The old coverage benchmark also requires unsupported/blocked/unverified rows to remain denominator-zero, so no alternative reading reaches 90%.\n\n## Smallest valid closure scope\n\nFirst freeze a reconciliation ledger, not a new feature list:\n\n1. Use every original P2-P6 requirement row as the starting set: P2 28 + P3 16 + P4 16 + P5 10 + P6 16 = **86 lane requirements**, then add the explicitly owned P1/runtime and competitor-surplus outcomes that are in the parent frozen scope. Deduplicate only by identical observable outcome and publish every merge/replacement mapping.\n2. For each row record: full contract, source provenance, implementation route, `complete | partial | missing | unsupported | test-pending`, composition recipe, and exact limitation. Keep unsupported and partial rows in the denominator.\n3. Recalculate. If the denominator were only the 94 non-replacement portfolio proxy, >=90% requires **85 implemented rows**, so at least **10 additional full rows** beyond the optimistic 75 are required. Because two current implemented rows are contract subsets and prefab apply is failing, the practical minimum is at least **13 full closures** unless the frozen mapping establishes otherwise.\n\nPrioritize the smallest high-value closure set already enabled by existing infrastructure:\n\n- **Composition closures:** previewSessionStart, previewSessionStop, skeletalAnimationPlay using existing runtimePreviewControl/runtimeSessionLifecycle/animationRuntimeControl, adding atomic postconditions and queue/session semantics where required.\n- **Repair near-complete:** prefabApplyOverrides, selective prefabRevertOverrides, full localizationValidate, animationRetargetValidate fixture/evidence.\n- **Bounded runtime adapters:** audioPlaybackControl, audioPlaybackObserve, animationGraphPreview, skeletalAnimationEvents.\n- **One authoring gap:** particleConfigure or renderConfigurationApply, whichever has a stable public Creator 3.7.3 mutation/read-back path.\n\nThat set is not permission to exclude the harder physics settings, bake, terrain, localization mutation/preview, render diagnostics, graph editing or preview-resolution rows. They remain denominator-zero and should move to Fixbug only after the reconciled calculation genuinely reaches >=90% and proportionate verification exists. At present, the evidence does not support closing the plan."
